.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH unarchive 1  "unarchive " 
.SH NAME
unarchive \- Unarchive one or more items, making them visible again. Cascades UP only: each item and its ancestor chain resurface, but its children/siblings stay archived. Partial per root; the result reports each root\*(Aqs outcome plus the full list of ids actually unarchived
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBunarchive\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIIDS\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Unarchive one or more items, making them visible again. Cascades UP only: each item and its ancestor chain resurface, but its children/siblings stay archived. Partial per root; the result reports each root\*(Aqs outcome plus the full list of ids actually unarchived
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIIDS\fR>
Item ids to unarchive (each surfaces its ancestor chain). At least one is required
